THE DEFECT AND ITS CAUSE
Reported by the user on visual inspection: the row action buttons stacked
vertically instead of sitting horizontally. Cause was flex-wrap on the action
group — once the "Confirm fees" text button widened the group beyond the
zero-width action column, the flex container wrapped each button onto its own
line. Static review had not caught it because the markup is individually
reasonable; only rendering shows the interaction between a w-0 column and a
wrapping flex child.

Wrapping was the wrong overflow strategy here regardless. The table is already
inside overflow-x-auto, so the narrow case should scroll within the container —
which is what workflow.md's responsive rule asks for — rather than reflow the
controls.

